questions.question_text:
Which point on the number line shows $\frac{14}{5}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0)--(6.5,0);
\foreach \x in {0,1,2,3,4} {\draw (1.5*\x,0.14)--(1.5*\x,-0.14); \node[below] at (1.5*\x,-0.16) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x in {0.5,1.5,2.5,3.5} {\draw (1.5*\x,0.08)--(1.5*\x,-0.08);}
\fill (0.54,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above] at (0.54,0.18) {$A$};
\fill (2.10,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above] at (2.10,0.18) {$B$};
\fill (3.60,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above] at (3.60,0.18) {$C$};
\fill (4.20,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above] at (4.20,0.18) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.solution_text:
$\frac{14}{5}=14\div5$
$=2.8$
That is eight tenths of the way from $2$ to $3$, which is point $D$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0)--(6.5,0);
\foreach \x in {0,1,2,3,4} {\draw (1.5*\x,0.14)--(1.5*\x,-0.14); \node[below] at (1.5*\x,-0.16) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x in {0.5,1.5,2.5,3.5} {\draw (1.5*\x,0.08)--(1.5*\x,-0.08);}
\fill (4.20,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above] at (4.20,0.18) {$\frac{14}{5}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

